CM WA5VJB (Kent Britain) "Cheap Yagi" - 11-element Yagi-Uda, 2450 MHz ISM
CM Source: Kent Britain, WA5VJB, "Cheap Yagis for 2450 MHz," CQ VHF,
CM Spring 2005, pp.37-40 (Table I, 11-element column). This IS a real,
CM published, measured amateur design - not a synthesized/derived
CM approximation like some other files in this set. Article-reported gain:
CM 12-13 dBi across the ham portion of the 2.4 GHz band (best match to a
CM "12 dBi 2.4 GHz Yagi" request of any design with public per-element
CM dimensions found).
CM
CM Table I dimensions (inches), reflector -> DE -> D1..D9, as published:
CM   Length:  2.4  2.2*  2.1  2.1  2.0  2.0  2.0  1.9  1.9  1.8  1.8
CM   Spacing: 0.0  0.6   1.3  2.1  3.0  4.2  5.2  6.2  7.3  8.5  9.8
CM   (spacing = cumulative distance from reflector, inches)
CM
CM *DRIVEN ELEMENT CAVEAT: in the original design the DE is not a plain
CM straight dipole - it's a flattened "J"/hairpin-folded element, about
CM 2.2" across (Figure 2 in the article), used as a gamma/hairpin-style
CM SWR matching structure: coax shield connects to the DE center, coax
CM center conductor to the inner tip of the J, with the J's free tip
CM trimmable for best SWR. This file simplifies that to a plain straight
CM 2.2" center-fed dipole (the standard simplification when porting a
CM hairpin-matched design into a basic wire-NEC model) - the far-field
CM gain/pattern should be close to the original, but the modeled feed
CM impedance/SWR will not exactly match the real hairpin-matched
CM hardware. The article itself notes the real build needed empirical SWR
CM tweaking even with the J-match in place.
CM
CM Real hardware: elements are 1/16" (0.0625" dia.) welding rod / 14 AWG
CM wire on a 1/4" wood or dowel boom. Boom dielectric effects (article
CM notes ~0.1" electrical shortening per inch of wood at these
CM frequencies) are not modeled here - free-space metal elements only,
CM consistent with the rest of this file set.
CM
CM Boom axis = X, elements along Y (HORIZONTAL polarization, matching the
CM article's photos), height Z = 6.0 m (change to match your mount).
CM Boresight = -X (toward directors), same convention as the other files
CM in this set. Feed = driven element (tag 2), center segment. Ground =
CM average (er=13, sigma=0.005 S/m) - swap GN line for another terrain.
